What is Glass Fiber Electronic Yarn?
Glass Fiber Electronic Yarn combines the structural advantages of conventional glass fiber with engineered dielectric properties that make it suitable for low‑loss, high‑frequency signal transmission. Unlike metallic conductors, the yarn maintains high tensile strength, low weight, and excellent resistance to corrosion and thermal cycling, which makes it an attractive alternative in environments where traditional copper bundles add unnecessary mass or suffer from fatigue.
